# Declare an API and participant

Create `contract.trellis` in the project from
[setup](/guides/write-a-service/setup):

```trellis
api "acme.orders@v1" {
    version "1.0.0";
    display_name "Orders";
    description "Minimal service walkthrough.";
    model CreateOrderRequest { customerId: string; }
    model CreateOrderResponse { orderId: string; customerId: string; }
    rpc "Orders.Create" {
        version "v1";
        input CreateOrderRequest;
        output CreateOrderResponse;
    }
}

participant "acme.orders-service" service {
    implements "acme.orders@v1";
}

api "acme.orders-caller@v1" {
    version "1.0.0";
    display_name "Orders caller";
    description "Caller for the service walkthrough.";
}

participant "acme.orders-caller" app {
    implements "acme.orders-caller@v1";
    use required orders "acme.orders@v1" {
        call rpc "Orders.Create";
    }
}
```

The first API defines the request and response. The service participant
implements it. The caller has its own identity and explicitly selects the one
action it will call; it does not gain permission merely by importing its types.
The empty caller-owned API is separate from the Orders API it consumes.

Generate the project:

```sh
trellis update
trellis generate
```

Because the project contains `deno.json`, generation emits TypeScript. A project
with `Cargo.toml` receives Rust crates; one with both manifests receives both.
There is no separate TypeScript contract execution or output stanza to
configure.

The provider participant is
`.trellis/ts/participants/acme-orders-service/mod.ts`; the caller is
`.trellis/ts/participants/acme-orders-caller/mod.ts`. API types and action
descriptors are exported by `.trellis/ts/apis/acme-orders/mod.ts`.

The API ID, participant ID, API release (`1.0.0`), and RPC transport version
(`v1`) are distinct. See [native IDL design](/design/contracts/trellis-idl) for
project and resolution semantics. This page is a minimal RPC example, not a
complete grammar reference; the operations, jobs, State, and store guides cover
their respective declarations.

Next, [implement the service](/guides/write-a-service/service-entrypoint).
